{{Top}}
{{Update|[[Queen's Shadow]]}}
{{Quote|<nowiki />''Time''. That's what's ''left'' when you strip away everything else. ''[&hellip;]'' From a certain perspective, time's the only thing a thief ever ''really'' steals. And it's the only ''gift'' an irredeemable disaster can give to anyone.|[[Chelli Lona Aphra]]|<ref name="Aphra 2016 40">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 40|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 40]]</ref>}}
[[File:Hourglass.png|thumb|right|200px|[[Hourglass]]es could be used to measure time.]]
'''Time''' was a measurable part of the structure of the [[universe]], in which [[the galaxy]] existed, where events occurred in a sequence. Time was measured with different concepts, such as [[Millennium|millennia]], [[Standard century|centuries]], and [[Standard year|years]]. Time could be broken down even further into [[Standard month|months]], [[Standard week|weeks]], [[Standard day|days]], [[Standard hour|hours]], [[Standard minute|minutes]], and [[second]]s, though these divisions were used almost exclusively to refer to the duration of events, rather than the date or time on which they took place. [[Chronometer]]s were used to track and indicate time through such units of measurement.<ref name="Weapons Factory">{{TCW|Weapons Factory}}</ref>

[[Time travel]] was a mostly hypothetical method of travel through time.<ref name="Rebels">{{Rebels|A World Between Worlds}}</ref> When traveling through hyperspace, the passage of time sped up, and [[Stasis field]]s were used to slow down time to match the rest of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Complete Vehicles, New Edition">''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''</ref> Time flowed differently in [[The Veil (Planet X)|the Veil]] than in normal space.<ref name="Path Ven">''[[The High Republic: Path of Vengeance]]''</ref>

==Time keeping==
===Overview===
{{Quote|Time, time, there's no ''time'' for time.|[[Inspector]] [[Tanivos Exantor Divo]]|<ref name="Senate Murders">{{TCW|Senate Murders}}</ref>}}
The last great conflict between the [[Jedi Order]] and the [[Sith]] resulted in a definitive Republic victory. Resetting its [[capital]] on [[Coruscant]], history reset its chrono on this date from which the modern Galactic Republic was born. The time before this rebirth was forgotten as a dark age, lumped into a collective whole known as the "[[Galactic Republic|Old Republic]]." As a result of this change, official calendars reset their zero year onto this date.<ref name="Propaganda">''[[Star Wars Propaganda: A History of Persuasive Art in the Galaxy]]''</ref> The galaxy used this standardized dating system based off of the galactic capital Coruscant:<ref name="Future of the Force Recon">{{RebelsRecon|sM_ZpTwSwuw|#2.09: Inside "The Future of the Force" &#124; Star Wars Rebels|sw_url=video/disneyxd-rebels-recon-inside-the-future-of-the-force}}</ref> the [[galactic standard calendar]]. On Coruscant, a year was made up of 365 days of 24 hours each,<ref name="AEYNK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> with no leap years.<ref name="SWCE 2016 DK Books Liveblog">{{SW|url=news/swce-2016-absolutely-everything-you-need-to-know-about-dk-star-wars-books-panel-liveblog|text=SWCE 2016: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know About DK ''Star Wars'' Books Panel Liveblog}}</ref>

During its [[Imperial Era|reign]], the [[Galactic Empire]] reset the dating system and utilized its own [[Imperial calendar|calendar]].<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> Sometime after the [[Battle of Yavin]], [[Ithorian]] [[artist]] [[Gammit Chond]] used a [[Galactic standard calendar|calendar system]] that used the battle as the zero year from which to date galactic history. Dates before the Battle of Yavin were marked "BBY" and dates after the Battle of Yavin were marked "ABY."<ref name="GA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> [[Galactic Standard Time]] was a system of timekeeping used by the [[First Order]].<ref name="Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens">{{Film|VII}}</ref> [[Lothal]] also maintained its own [[Lothal Calendar|calendar]].<ref name="AEYNK" />

===Units of time===
The most commonly used measurements of time in the Galaxy were the '''day''' and the '''year''', both based on the orbital characteristics of Coruscant.<ref name="Future of the Force Recon">{{RebelsRecon|sM_ZpTwSwuw|#2.09: Inside "The Future of the Force" &#124; Star Wars Rebels|sw_url=video/disneyxd-rebels-recon-inside-the-future-of-the-force}}</ref> The day was based on its rotational period, and the year was based on its orbital period which, due to a convenient coincidence, was ''exactly'' 365 times its rotational period. The day was subdivided into 24 '''hour'''s.<ref name="AB Update">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> A minute was 60 '''second'''s.<ref name="Star Wars (2020) 18">[[Star Wars (2020) 18|''Star Wars'' (2020) 18]]</ref>

===Ancient time keeping methods===
Long before the modern Galactic Republic, the [[Domancion Accord]] was used as the zero year for an ancient dating system.<ref name="Doctor Aphra 6">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 6|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 6]]</ref>

The [[Coruscant reckoning calendar|C.R.C.]] was another dating system that set its epoch 7977 years before the [[Galactic Empire]] issued an arrest warrant for [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] after discovering she worked with the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="Scum and Villainy Case Files">''[[Star Wars: Scum and Villainy: Case Files on the Galaxy's Most Notorious]]''</ref>

